What was changed
----------------

  * Android/Termux support (the reason for the fork):
      - `target_os = "linux"` cfg gates widened to
        `any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "android")` where the underlying
        facility exists on Bionic.
      - A new runtime-directory resolver, `rmux_os::runtime_dir`, replacing
        hardcoded `/tmp` — Termux is not FHS.
      - `rmux-pty` uses the `ptsname` path on Android (rustix exposes no
        `TIOCGPTPEER` binding there).
      - `rmux-client`'s SIGWINCH watcher uses the `signal-hook` backend on
        Android (`rustix::runtime` does not exist on rustix's libc backend).
      - `nl_langinfo` replaced with a constant on Android (Bionic is UTF-8 only
        and `libc` binds neither `nl_langinfo` nor `CODESET` there).

  * The binaries are renamed `kmux` and `kmux-daemon`. Executable names are now
    sourced from `rmux_os::host` (now `kmux::os::host`) rather than being spelled
    inline.

  * Single-crate collapse. Upstream rmux is a workspace of many crates, and this
    fork originally nested them under `crates/kmux/crates/` (rmux-client,
    rmux-core, rmux-ipc, rmux-os, rmux-proto, rmux-pty, rmux-sdk, rmux-server,
    rmux-types, rmux-web-crypto, plus the unused integration crates
    ratatui-rmux and rmux-render-core). To publish to crates.io WITHOUT squatting
    upstream rmux's crate names, those ten sub-crates the `kmux` binary needs were
    folded into ONE self-contained `kmux` crate as the intra-crate modules
    `client`, `core`, `ipc`, `os`, `proto`, `pty`, `sdk`, `server`, `types`, and
    `web_crypto` (see `src/lib.rs`). Every cross-crate path `rmux_core::X` became
    `crate::core::X` (and `kmux::core::X` from the binaries), each sub-crate's
    `lib.rs` became a module `mod.rs`, and the sub-crates' Cargo manifests were
    unioned into this one. `ratatui-rmux` and `rmux-render-core` were dropped
    (nothing in the `kmux` binary links them). The former `rmux-server` build
    script (tunnel-preset codegen) was merged into this crate's `build.rs`. The
    package is `publish = true` at version 0.1.0; the library keeps the name
    `kmux`. Upstream dependency pins were carried verbatim.

Upstream's own release/packaging/CI scripts, benchmarks, `xtask`, and
contributor documentation were not carried into the fork.
